# Enzyme-substrate motif with two conservation laws whose dependent-species
# choice used to be ill-posed (issue #63 follow-up).
#
#   X(p~0) + Y <-> X(p~0).Y -> X(p~1) + Y,   X(p~1) -> X(p~0)
#
# Conserved: Xtotal = X0 + Xp + XY and Ytotal = Y + XY. Both laws constrain XY,
# so picking each law's dependent independently (largest |coefficient| not
# already claimed) can land on a pair for which L[:, dependent] is SINGULAR --
# the elimination "solve law k for y[dep_k]" then has no solution, and every
# consumer of the reduction (reconstruct_full, the sensitivity D matrix) silently
# produces a state that violates the constraints it is enforcing.
#
# Distilled from rulehub Tutorials/simplesystem, the smallest of the 66 corpus
# models that hit this. Kept tiny so the invariant is checkable by hand.
begin parameters
    1 kon        10  # Constant
    2 koff       5  # Constant
    3 kcat       0.7  # Constant
    4 dephos     0.5  # Constant
end parameters
begin species
    1 X(p~0,y) 5000
    2 X(p~1,y) 0
    3 Y(x) 500
    4 X(p~0,y!1).Y(x!1) 0
end species
begin reactions
    1 1,3 4 kon #_R1
    2 2 1 dephos #_R4
    3 4 1,3 koff #_R2
    4 4 2,3 kcat #_R3
end reactions
begin groups
    1 X_free               1
    2 X_p_total            2
    3 Xp_free              2
    4 XY                   4
    5 Ytotal               3,4
    6 Xtotal               1,2,4
end groups
